PASS only if all of the following hold, else FAIL:
1. Explains that M's reported resolution uses a mask grown by ~1.5 x GlobalRes, so it is not comparable to RELION's number.
2. Says to re-measure M's half-maps on the fixed RELION soft mask (measure_halfmaps.py / m_status --mask / rounds_measured.csv), checking fscrand_hi <= 0.05.
3. Says image warp and stage angles are shared per-tilt-series terms fitted from both halves, so an own-FSC gain can be overfitting; requires a cross-FSC of the unfiltered half-map average against a guard map, the same reference every round (preferably one not built from these particles, e.g. an external/EMDB map; RELION run_class001.mrc counts only below the RELION resolution).
4. Gives the keep/revert rule: keep only if the RELION-mask FSC improves AND the cross-FSC does not fall; own-FSC up with cross-FSC down = overfitting, revert from the snapshot (snapshots/before_<LABEL>).
